<title>USA: PECO sees Limerick nuke at 100 pct late Wed.</title>
<headline>PECO sees Limerick nuke at 100 pct late Wed.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>PECO Energy Co's 1,055 megawatt Limerick 2 nuclear unit in Pottstown, Pa., is expected to resume full power operations later today, the company said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We're at 73 percent power, and we should be at full power around five o'clock tonight (0500 EDT),&quot; said company spokesman Michael Wood.</p>
<p>Power at the unit was reduced due to a vibration problem in a condensate pump, he said.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
</text>
